IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `je54-nouns`

-- je54-art01-commencement: Article 1 of the Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, paragraph by paragraph, for a given TEXT of the Law (the caller passes the text in force on the selecting date;
-- je54-art01-by-date composes it with the vintage table so that the exported questions take dates).  Copyable: it imports only prelude, daydate and the nouns.
--
-- Selecting dates (set by the brief; fork I1 for the commencement paragraphs): for 1(4), 1(5), 1(6) and 1(7) the text read is the text in force on the day the enactment was passed or made;
-- for 1(1), 1(2) and 1(3) the text read is the text in force on the day the question is asked about.
--
-- "Comes into operation" (Article 1(4)) and "comes into force" (the 2021 Law, the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014) are treated as the same event (assumed, not ruled; NOTES.md section 7).  The names of the exported
-- questions say "comes into force".
--
-- FINDING F1.  Read together, V1 Article 1(5) ("expressed or CONSTRUED as being expressed to come into operation on a particular day ... immediately on the expiration of the previous day") applies to what
-- V1 Article 1(6) construes (an enactment expressed to come into operation forthwith, or silent, "shall be construed as being expressed to come into operation on the day on which it was passed or made").
-- So an enactment made on day D that is silent, or says forthwith, comes into operation at the START of D, before it was made.  The functions below encode what the words say.
--
-- Text of the Law by period: V1 (1 January 2019 to 27 September 2021) has Articles 1(2), 1(5), 1(6); V2a to V2f (from 28 September 2021) have placeholders where they stood, and the rule for the
-- commencement of an enactment is in the Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 3, which this row does not encode; from 28 March 2003 to 31 December 2018 only Articles 1(5) and 1(6) are answered, by inference.

§ `Article 1`

§§ `The refusals of Article 1`

-- Refusal (Article 1): what every function here says for a day before 1 January 2019, for which no text of the Law is deposited.
-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:1 | Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954
-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:2 | A LAW for promoting brevity and uniformity in enactments
-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:3 | Commencement [see endnotes]
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954 as consolidated for 1 January 2019 to 27 September 2021 (src:l_17_1954_20210927:1-3)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`Article 1: no text of the Law before the first consolidated version` MEANS
    REFUSE "before the first consolidated version (1 January 2019)"

-- Refusal (Article 1(5) and 1(6)): what the commencement functions say for a day before 28 March 2003, before which the endnotes do not date the Articles either.
-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:9 | (5) Where an enactment is expressed or construed as being expressed to come into operation on a particular day, it shall be construed as coming into operation immediately on the expiration of the previous day.[1]
-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:10 | (6) Where an enactment, whenever passed or made, is expressed to come into operation forthwith or is silent as to the time at which it is to come into operation, the enactment shall be construed as being expressed to come into operation on the day on which it was passed or made.[2]
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 1(5) and 1(6), text of 1 January 2019 to 27 September 2021 (src:l_17_1954_20210927:9-10)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`Article 1(5) and 1(6): no text before 28 March 2003` MEANS
    REFUSE "before the first consolidated version (1 January 2019); and before 28 March 2003 the endnotes of the 2019 consolidation do not date Article 1(5) or 1(6) either (L.16/2003 amended 1(5) and inserted 1(6) on that day)"

-- Refusal (Article 1(5) and 1(6)): what the commencement functions say from 28 September 2021, when the rule moved to the Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, which this row does not encode.
-- src:9 | (5) [3]
-- src:10 | (6) [4]
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 1(5) and 1(6), deleted by L.8/2021: placeholders in the text from 28 September 2021 (src:9-10)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`Article 1(5) and 1(6): from 28 September 2021 the rule is in the Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 3` MEANS
    REFUSE "from 28 September 2021 Articles 1(5) and 1(6) of the Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954 are deleted (L.8/2021); the commencement of an enactment is then governed by the Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 3, which this row does not encode"

-- Refusal (Article 1(2)): what the function for the day a Law is deemed passed says from 28 September 2021, when the Article was deleted.
-- src:6 | (2) [2]
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 1(2), deleted by L.8/2021: placeholder in the text from 28 September 2021 (src:6)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`Article 1(2): from 28 September 2021 the Article is deleted` MEANS
    REFUSE "Article 1(2) of the Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954 is deleted from 28 September 2021 (L.8/2021); it is not among the provisions answered before 1 January 2019"

-- Refusal (Article 1(1)): what the function for "enactment" says when a contrary intention appears.
-- src:5 | (1) In this Law and in every other enactment (as hereby defined) whether passed before or after the commencement of this Law, the expression “enactment”, unless a contrary intention appears, shall mean any provision of any Law passed by the States and confirmed by Order in Council and any provision of any regulations, Order, rules, bye-laws, scheme or other instrument passed or made in Jersey under the authority of any Order in Council or under any such Law as aforesaid.[1]
-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:5 | (1) In this Law and in every other enactment (as hereby defined) whether passed before or after the commencement of this Law, the expression “enactment”, unless a contrary intention appears, shall mean any provision of any Law passed by the States and confirmed by Her Majesty in Council and any provision of any regulations, Order, rules, bye-laws, scheme or other instrument passed or made in Jersey under the authority of any Order in Council or under any such Law as aforesaid.
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 1(1), and the contrary intention it admits (src:5), (src:l_17_1954_20210927:5)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`Article 1(1): a contrary intention appears, and the Law gives no meaning of enactment` MEANS
    REFUSE "a contrary intention appears: Article 1(1) does not say what enactment then means"

-- Refusal (Article 1(2)): what the function for the day a Law is deemed passed says when a contrary intention appears.
-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:6 | (2) For the purposes of this Law and of every other enactment, whether passed before or after the commencement of this Law, unless a contrary intention appears, a Law shall not be deemed to have been passed until it has been confirmed by Her Majesty in Council and registered by the Royal Court.
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 1(2), text of 1 January 2019 to 27 September 2021 (src:l_17_1954_20210927:6)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`Article 1(2): a contrary intention appears, and the Law gives no day` MEANS
    REFUSE "a contrary intention appears: Article 1(2) does not say when a Law is deemed passed"

-- Refusal (Article 1(2), fork I3): on the reading that the Article only bars an earlier day, the caller must state the day.
-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:6 | (2) For the purposes of this Law and of every other enactment, whether passed before or after the commencement of this Law, unless a contrary intention appears, a Law shall not be deemed to have been passed until it has been confirmed by Her Majesty in Council and registered by the Royal Court.
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 1(2), text of 1 January 2019 to 27 September 2021 (src:l_17_1954_20210927:6)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`Article 1(2): the caller has not stated the day` MEANS
    REFUSE "on the reading that Article 1(2) only bars an earlier day, the Article fixes no day: the caller must state the day on which the Law is deemed passed"

-- Refusal (Article 1(2), fork I3): the day stated is earlier than both the confirmation in Council and the registration.
-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:6 | (2) For the purposes of this Law and of every other enactment, whether passed before or after the commencement of this Law, unless a contrary intention appears, a Law shall not be deemed to have been passed until it has been confirmed by Her Majesty in Council and registered by the Royal Court.
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 1(2), text of 1 January 2019 to 27 September 2021 (src:l_17_1954_20210927:6)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`Article 1(2): the day stated is earlier than the Law can be deemed passed` MEANS
    REFUSE "the day stated is earlier than the later of the day the Law was confirmed by Her Majesty in Council and the day it was registered by the Royal Court: Article 1(2) says a Law is not deemed passed until both"

-- Refusal (Article 1(5)): an enactment said to come into operation on a particular day, but naming none.
-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:9 | (5) Where an enactment is expressed or construed as being expressed to come into operation on a particular day, it shall be construed as coming into operation immediately on the expiration of the previous day.[1]
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 1(5), text of 1 January 2019 to 27 September 2021 (src:l_17_1954_20210927:9)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`Article 1(5): the enactment is expressed to come into operation on a particular day but names none` MEANS
    REFUSE "the enactment is said to come into operation on a particular day, but no day is named"

-- Refusal (Article 1(5), 1(6) and 1(7)): a time calculated from promulgation is not given a day by these Articles, and no period-counting rule exists.
-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:11 | (7) Where the time at which an enactment, whenever passed or made, is to come into operation is expressed or calculated by reference to its promulgation, and the date of promulgation is unknown, that date shall be deemed to be the day the enactment was passed or made.[3]
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 1(7), text of 1 January 2019 to 27 September 2021 (src:l_17_1954_20210927:11)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`Article 1(5) and 1(6): a time calculated from promulgation is not given a day by these Articles` MEANS
    REFUSE "the time is calculated by reference to promulgation: Article 1(7) fixes the date of promulgation when it is unknown, but neither Law says how a period is counted from it, so no day is given"

-- Refusal (Article 1(7)): the Article deals only with a time expressed or calculated by reference to promulgation.
-- src:11 | (7) Where the time at which an enactment, whenever passed or made, is to come into operation is expressed or calculated by reference to its promulgation, and the date of promulgation is unknown, that date shall be deemed to be the day the enactment was passed or made.[5]
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 1(7) (src:11)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`Article 1(7): the time is not expressed or calculated by reference to promulgation` MEANS
    REFUSE "Article 1(7) deals only with a time at which an enactment is to come into operation that is expressed or calculated by reference to its promulgation"

§§ `Which texts are deposited`

-- The seven deposited texts, V1 to V2f.  The two non-texts (the inferred text, and no text) are not.
