GIVEN v IS A `Text of the Law`
GIVETH A `Basis of a reading`
`Article 1: the basis on which the text of the Law is read` v MEANS
    CONSIDER v
    WHEN `the inferred text from 28 March 2003 to 31 December 2018` THEN `inferred from the endnotes of the 2019 consolidation, not verified against L.16/2003`
    OTHERWISE `read from the deposited text in force on that day`

§§ `Article 1(1): what an enactment is`

-- Article 1(1): whether a kind of instrument is one that the Law calls an enactment.
-- src:5 | (1) In this Law and in every other enactment (as hereby defined) whether passed before or after the commencement of this Law, the expression “enactment”, unless a contrary intention appears, shall mean any provision of any Law passed by the States and confirmed by Order in Council and any provision of any regulations, Order, rules, bye-laws, scheme or other instrument passed or made in Jersey under the authority of any Order in Council or under any such Law as aforesaid.[1]
-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:5 | (1) In this Law and in every other enactment (as hereby defined) whether passed before or after the commencement of this Law, the expression “enactment”, unless a contrary intention appears, shall mean any provision of any Law passed by the States and confirmed by Her Majesty in Council and any provision of any regulations, Order, rules, bye-laws, scheme or other instrument passed or made in Jersey under the authority of any Order in Council or under any such Law as aforesaid.
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 1(1) (src:5), (src:l_17_1954_20210927:5)
GIVEN k IS A `Kind of instrument`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the instrument is a kind that Article 1(1) calls an enactment` k MEANS
    CONSIDER k
    WHEN `a Law passed by the States and confirmed in Council` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `regulations, an Order, rules, bye-laws, a scheme or other instrument passed or made in Jersey under the authority of an Order in Council` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `regulations, an Order, rules, bye-laws, a scheme or other instrument passed or made in Jersey under a Law passed by the States and confirmed in Council` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `something that is none of these` THEN FALSE

-- Selecting date: the day the question is asked about.  Every text from V1 reads alike for this paragraph (V1, V2a to V2c say "confirmed by Her Majesty in Council"; V2d to V2f say "confirmed by Order in Council",
-- an editorial revision of 11 January 2024), so the text only decides whether there is a text; before 1 January 2019 the paragraph refuses.  Whether "Her Majesty" in the older wording covers a confirmation made by His Majesty
-- is not answered by the Law (NOTES.md section 10).
-- src:5 | (1) In this Law and in every other enactment (as hereby defined) whether passed before or after the commencement of this Law, the expression “enactment”, unless a contrary intention appears, shall mean any provision of any Law passed by the States and confirmed by Order in Council and any provision of any regulations, Order, rules, bye-laws, scheme or other instrument passed or made in Jersey under the authority of any Order in Council or under any such Law as aforesaid.[1]
-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:5 | (1) In this Law and in every other enactment (as hereby defined) whether passed before or after the commencement of this Law, the expression “enactment”, unless a contrary intention appears, shall mean any provision of any Law passed by the States and confirmed by Her Majesty in Council and any provision of any regulations, Order, rules, bye-laws, scheme or other instrument passed or made in Jersey under the authority of any Order in Council or under any such Law as aforesaid.
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 1(1) (src:5), (src:l_17_1954_20210927:5)
GIVEN v IS A `Text of the Law`
      k IS A `Kind of instrument`
      `a contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 1(1): the instrument is an enactment` v k `a contrary intention appears` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT `Article 1: the text of the Law is a deposited text` v THEN `Article 1: no text of the Law before the first consolidated version`
           IF `a contrary intention appears` THEN `Article 1(1): a contrary intention appears, and the Law gives no meaning of enactment`
           OTHERWISE `the instrument is a kind that Article 1(1) calls an enactment` k

§§ `Article 1(2): when a Law is passed (the text of 1 January 2019 to 27 September 2021 only)`

-- Fork I3.  Reading 1 (taken): "a Law shall not be deemed to have been passed until it has been confirmed by Her Majesty in Council and registered by the Royal Court" fixes the day: the later of the two days.
-- Reading 2: the words only bar an earlier day and fix none; the caller states the day, and it must not be earlier than both.
-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:6 | (2) For the purposes of this Law and of every other enactment, whether passed before or after the commencement of this Law, unless a contrary intention appears, a Law shall not be deemed to have been passed until it has been confirmed by Her Majesty in Council and registered by the Royal Court.
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 1(2), text of 1 January 2019 to 27 September 2021 (src:l_17_1954_20210927:6)
GIVEN confirmed IS A DATE
      registered IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the later of the day a Law was confirmed in Council and the day it was registered` confirmed registered MEANS
    IF confirmed AT LEAST registered THEN confirmed ELSE registered

-- Article 1(2), fork I3: the day a Law is deemed passed on each reading of the Article.
-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:6 | (2) For the purposes of this Law and of every other enactment, whether passed before or after the commencement of this Law, unless a contrary intention appears, a Law shall not be deemed to have been passed until it has been confirmed by Her Majesty in Council and registered by the Royal Court.
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 1(2), text of 1 January 2019 to 27 September 2021 (src:l_17_1954_20210927:6)
GIVEN confirmed IS A DATE
      registered IS A DATE
      reading IS A `Reading of Article 1(2)`
      stated IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day on which a Law is deemed passed on this reading of Article 1(2)` confirmed registered reading stated MEANS
    CONSIDER reading
    WHEN `the Law is deemed passed on the later of the day it was confirmed and the day it was registered` THEN
        `the later of the day a Law was confirmed in Council and the day it was registered` confirmed registered
    WHEN `the Article only bars an earlier day: the caller states the day` THEN
        CONSIDER stated
        WHEN NOTHING THEN `Article 1(2): the caller has not stated the day`
        WHEN JUST day THEN
            IF day AT LEAST `the later of the day a Law was confirmed in Council and the day it was registered` confirmed registered
            THEN day
            ELSE `Article 1(2): the day stated is earlier than the Law can be deemed passed`

-- Article 1(2): the day on which a Law is deemed passed, in the text of 1 January 2019 to 27 September 2021 only.
-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:6 | (2) For the purposes of this Law and of every other enactment, whether passed before or after the commencement of this Law, unless a contrary intention appears, a Law shall not be deemed to have been passed until it has been confirmed by Her Majesty in Council and registered by the Royal Court.
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 1(2), text of 1 January 2019 to 27 September 2021 (src:l_17_1954_20210927:6)
GIVEN v IS A `Text of the Law`
      `the day it was confirmed by Her Majesty in Council` IS A DATE
      `the day it was registered by the Royal Court` IS A DATE
      reading IS A `Reading of Article 1(2)` TYPICALLY `the Law is deemed passed on the later of the day it was confirmed and the day it was registered`
      `the day the caller states` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `a contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DATE
`Article 1(2): the day on which a Law is deemed passed` v `the day it was confirmed by Her Majesty in Council` `the day it was registered by the Royal Court` reading `the day the caller states` `a contrary intention appears` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT `Article 1: the text of the Law is a deposited text` v THEN `Article 1: no text of the Law before the first consolidated version`
           IF NOT (v EQUALS `V1, 1 January 2019 to 27 September 2021`) THEN `Article 1(2): from 28 September 2021 the Article is deleted`
           IF `a contrary intention appears` THEN `Article 1(2): a contrary intention appears, and the Law gives no day`
           OTHERWISE `the day on which a Law is deemed passed on this reading of Article 1(2)` `the day it was confirmed by Her Majesty in Council` `the day it was registered by the Royal Court` reading `the day the caller states`

§§ `Article 1(3): passing and repeal, making and rescission`

-- Article 1(3): how a reference to passing or repeal is read, apart from the text.
-- src:7 | (3) In this Law and in every other enactment, whether passed before or after the commencement of this Law, references to the passing or repeal of an enactment shall be construed, where appropriate, as references to the making or rescission of that enactment.
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 1(3) (src:7)
GIVEN word IS A `Word read by Article 1(3)`
      `it is appropriate to read it so` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Reading under Article 1(3)`
`the reading of a reference to passing or repeal under Article 1(3)` word `it is appropriate to read it so` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT `it is appropriate to read it so` THEN `as written`
           OTHERWISE
               CONSIDER word
               WHEN `passing` THEN `as a reference to the making of the enactment`
               WHEN `repeal` THEN `as a reference to the rescission of the enactment`

-- Article 1(3): how a reference to the passing or the repeal of an enactment is read, for a given text of the Law.
-- src:7 | (3) In this Law and in every other enactment, whether passed before or after the commencement of this Law, references to the passing or repeal of an enactment shall be construed, where appropriate, as references to the making or rescission of that enactment.
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 1(3) (src:7)
GIVEN v IS A `Text of the Law`
      word IS A `Word read by Article 1(3)`
      `it is appropriate to read it so` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Reading under Article 1(3)`
`Article 1(3): how a reference to passing or repeal is read` v word `it is appropriate to read it so` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT `Article 1: the text of the Law is a deposited text` v THEN `Article 1: no text of the Law before the first consolidated version`
           OTHERWISE `the reading of a reference to passing or repeal under Article 1(3)` word `it is appropriate to read it so`

§§ `Articles 1(4), 1(5) and 1(6): the time at which an enactment comes into operation`

-- The day on which the enactment is construed as coming into operation (it comes into operation at the start of that day: 1(5), "immediately on the expiration of the previous day").
-- Under 1(5): an enactment expressed to come into operation on a particular day.  Under 1(6): one expressed to come into operation forthwith, or silent, is construed as expressed to come into operation on
-- the day on which it was passed or made, and then 1(5) applies to it (FINDING F1).  An enactment whose time is calculated by reference to its promulgation is not given a day by these Articles.
-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:9 | (5) Where an enactment is expressed or construed as being expressed to come into operation on a particular day, it shall be construed as coming into operation immediately on the expiration of the previous day.[1]
-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:10 | (6) Where an enactment, whenever passed or made, is expressed to come into operation forthwith or is silent as to the time at which it is to come into operation, the enactment shall be construed as being expressed to come into operation on the day on which it was passed or made.[2]
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 1(5) and 1(6), text of 1 January 2019 to 27 September 2021 (src:l_17_1954_20210927:9-10)
GIVEN c IS A `Commencement as stated`
      basis IS A `Basis of a reading`
GIVETH A `Day with its basis`
`Article 1(5) and 1(6): the day under the text` c basis MEANS
    CONSIDER c's `how it is expressed`
    WHEN `on a particular day` THEN
        CONSIDER c's `the day it names`
        WHEN JUST named THEN `Day with its basis` WITH `the day` IS named, `the basis` IS basis
        WHEN NOTHING THEN `Article 1(5): the enactment is expressed to come into operation on a particular day but names none`
    WHEN `forthwith` THEN `Day with its basis` WITH `the day` IS c's `the day it was passed or made`, `the basis` IS basis
    WHEN `silent as to the time at which it is to come into operation` THEN `Day with its basis` WITH `the day` IS c's `the day it was passed or made`, `the basis` IS basis
    WHEN `calculated by reference to its promulgation` THEN `Article 1(5) and 1(6): a time calculated from promulgation is not given a day by these Articles`

-- v is the text in force on the day the enactment was passed or made (fork I1 chooses another selecting date in je54-art01-by-date).
-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:9 | (5) Where an enactment is expressed or construed as being expressed to come into operation on a particular day, it shall be construed as coming into operation immediately on the expiration of the previous day.[1]
-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:10 | (6) Where an enactment, whenever passed or made, is expressed to come into operation forthwith or is silent as to the time at which it is to come into operation, the enactment shall be construed as being expressed to come into operation on the day on which it was passed or made.[2]
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 1(5) and 1(6), text of 1 January 2019 to 27 September 2021 (src:l_17_1954_20210927:9-10)
GIVEN v IS A `Text of the Law`
      c IS A `Commencement as stated`
GIVETH A `Day with its basis`
`Article 1(5) and 1(6): the day on which the enactment comes into operation` v c MEANS
    CONSIDER v
    WHEN `no text before 28 March 2003` THEN `Article 1(5) and 1(6): no text before 28 March 2003`
    WHEN `the inferred text from 28 March 2003 to 31 December 2018` THEN
        `Article 1(5) and 1(6): the day under the text` c `inferred from the endnotes of the 2019 consolidation, not verified against L.16/2003`
    WHEN `V1, 1 January 2019 to 27 September 2021` THEN
        `Article 1(5) and 1(6): the day under the text` c `read from the deposited text in force on that day`
    OTHERWISE `Article 1(5) and 1(6): from 28 September 2021 the rule is in the Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 3`

-- Article 1(4): the moment at which an enactment comes into operation: the start of the day found under Articles 1(5) and 1(6), on the clock of the zone given.
-- src:8 | (4) In this Law and in every other enactment, whether passed before or after the commencement of this Law, the expression “commencement”, when used with reference to an enactment, shall mean the time at which the enactment comes into operation.
-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:9 | (5) Where an enactment is expressed or construed as being expressed to come into operation on a particular day, it shall be construed as coming into operation immediately on the expiration of the previous day.[1]
-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:10 | (6) Where an enactment, whenever passed or made, is expressed to come into operation forthwith or is silent as to the time at which it is to come into operation, the enactment shall be construed as being expressed to come into operation on the day on which it was passed or made.[2]
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 1(4): commencement is the time at which the enactment comes into operation (src:8); Article 1(5) and 1(6) (src:l_17_1954_20210927:9-10)
GIVEN v IS A `Text of the Law`
      c IS A `Commencement as stated`
      zone IS A STRING
GIVETH A `Moment with its basis`
`Article 1(4): the commencement of the enactment, the moment at which it comes into operation` v c zone MEANS
    LET r MEANS `Article 1(5) and 1(6): the day on which the enactment comes into operation` v c IN
        `Moment with its basis` WITH
            `the moment` IS DATETIME_FROM_DTZ (r's `the day`) (TIME_FROM_HMS 0 0 0) zone
            `the basis` IS r's `the basis`

-- Article 1(4): whether an enactment is in force on a given day.
-- src:8 | (4) In this Law and in every other enactment, whether passed before or after the commencement of this Law, the expression “commencement”, when used with reference to an enactment, shall mean the time at which the enactment comes into operation.
-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:9 | (5) Where an enactment is expressed or construed as being expressed to come into operation on a particular day, it shall be construed as coming into operation immediately on the expiration of the previous day.[1]
-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:10 | (6) Where an enactment, whenever passed or made, is expressed to come into operation forthwith or is silent as to the time at which it is to come into operation, the enactment shall be construed as being expressed to come into operation on the day on which it was passed or made.[2]
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 1(4) (src:8); Article 1(5) and 1(6) (src:l_17_1954_20210927:9-10)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
      v IS A `Text of the Law`
      c IS A `Commencement as stated`
GIVETH A `Yes or no with its basis`
`Article 1(4): the enactment is in force on` d `under` v c MEANS
    LET r MEANS `Article 1(5) and 1(6): the day on which the enactment comes into operation` v c IN
        `Yes or no with its basis` WITH
            `the answer` IS d AT LEAST r's `the day`
            `the basis` IS r's `the basis`

-- Article 1(4): whether an enactment is in force at a given moment.
-- src:8 | (4) In this Law and in every other enactment, whether passed before or after the commencement of this Law, the expression “commencement”, when used with reference to an enactment, shall mean the time at which the enactment comes into operation.
-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:9 | (5) Where an enactment is expressed or construed as being expressed to come into operation on a particular day, it shall be construed as coming into operation immediately on the expiration of the previous day.[1]
-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:10 | (6) Where an enactment, whenever passed or made, is expressed to come into operation forthwith or is silent as to the time at which it is to come into operation, the enactment shall be construed as being expressed to come into operation on the day on which it was passed or made.[2]
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 1(4) (src:8); Article 1(5) and 1(6) (src:l_17_1954_20210927:9-10)
GIVEN t IS A DATETIME
      zone IS A STRING
      v IS A `Text of the Law`
      c IS A `Commencement as stated`
GIVETH A `Yes or no with its basis`
`Article 1(4): the enactment is in force at` t `in the zone` zone `under` v c MEANS
    LET r MEANS `Article 1(4): the commencement of the enactment, the moment at which it comes into operation` v c zone IN
        `Yes or no with its basis` WITH
            `the answer` IS DATETIME_SERIAL t AT LEAST DATETIME_SERIAL (r's `the moment`)
            `the basis` IS r's `the basis`

§§ `Article 1(7): the date of promulgation when it is unknown`

-- All seven deposited texts say the same; before 1 January 2019 the paragraph refuses (it is not one of the four provisions answered by inference).
-- Selecting date: the day the enactment was passed or made.  "Whenever passed or made": no date bars an enactment from it.
-- src:11 | (7) Where the time at which an enactment, whenever passed or made, is to come into operation is expressed or calculated by reference to its promulgation, and the date of promulgation is unknown, that date shall be deemed to be the day the enactment was passed or made.[5]
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 1(7) (src:11)
GIVEN v IS A `Text of the Law`
      `the time is expressed or calculated by reference to promulgation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of promulgation` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the day the enactment was passed or made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`Article 1(7): the date of promulgation to be used` v `the time is expressed or calculated by reference to promulgation` `the date of promulgation` `the day the enactment was passed or made` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT `Article 1: the text of the Law is a deposited text` v THEN `Article 1: no text of the Law before the first consolidated version`
           IF NOT `the time is expressed or calculated by reference to promulgation` THEN `Article 1(7): the time is not expressed or calculated by reference to promulgation`
           OTHERWISE
               CONSIDER `the date of promulgation`
               WHEN JUST known THEN known
               WHEN NOTHING THEN `the day the enactment was passed or made`
